Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:20:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Compose GLM DFlash pages with SparkCache contracts

The GLM-5.3 DFlash page-geometry and FlashKDA stack now retains SparkCache clean-recompute handling, shared-prefix leases, recurrent boundary ownership, partial-tail publication targets, and draft-specific load configuration.

The composition is based on local-inference-lab/vllm PR 535 at ead9d8a4. It changes no SparkCache wire identity directly; the PR stack's page geometry must produce a distinct topology-bound cache identity during deployment.

Validation: Ruff 0.14.0 check and formatting pass. The Linux ARM64 CUDA runtime passed 199 focused recurrent-boundary, page-geometry, cache-planning, and DFlash tests.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Signed-off-by: FujitsuPolycom <87842395+FujitsuPolycom@users.noreply.github.com>
